{"id":"mahabharata-3-180","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":180,"title":"अशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 180 · Krishna and Markandeya come to Kamyaka","summary":{"en":"In the Kamyaka forest Krishna visits with Satyabhama, praises Arjuna and tells of Draupadi's sons growing up at Dvaraka. The ancient sage Markandeya also arrives, and the Pandavas and Krishna ask him to tell them the old stories.","kn":"ಕಾಮ್ಯಕವನದಲ್ಲಿ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಸತ್ಯಭಾಮೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಬಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳಿ ದ್ವಾರಕೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಬೆಳೆಯುತ್ತಿರುವ ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯ ಮಕ್ಕಳ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಋಷಿ ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರೂ ಬರುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣರು ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಕಥೆಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳೆಂದು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"काम्यक वन में श्रीकृष्ण सत्यभामा के साथ आते हैं, अर्जुन की प्रशंसा करते हैं और द्वारका में बढ़ते द्रौपदी के पुत्रों की बात बताते हैं। प्राचीन ऋषि मार्कण्डेय भी आते हैं, और पाण्डव तथा श्रीकृष्ण उनसे पुरानी कथाएँ सुनाने को कहते हैं।","te":"కామ్యకవనంలో శ్రీకృష్ణుడు సత్యభామతో వచ్చి అర్జునుని కొనియాడి ద్వారకలో పెరుగుతున్న ద్రౌపది కుమారుల గురించి చెబుతాడు. ప్రాచీన ఋషి మార్కండేయుడు కూడా వస్తాడు; పాండవులు, శ్రీకృష్ణుడు పాత కథలు చెప్పమని అడుగుతారు.","ta":"காம்யக வனத்தில் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் ஸத்யபாமாவுடன் வந்து அர்ஜுனனைப் புகழ்ந்து, த்வாரகையில் வளரும் திரௌபதியின் மைந்தர்களைப் பற்றிச் சொல்கிறார். பழமையான மார்க்கண்டேய முனிவரும் வர, பாண்டவர்களும் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரும் பழங்கதைகளைச் சொல்லுமாறு கேட்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"കാമ്യകവനത്തിൽ സത്യഭാമയോടൊപ്പം കൃഷ്ണൻ സന്ദർശിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനനെ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു, ദ്വാരകയിൽ വളരുന്ന ദ്രൗപദിയുടെ പുത്രന്മാരെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയുന്നു. പുരാതന മുനിയായ മാർക്കണ്ഡേയനും എത്തുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവരും കൃഷ്ണനും പഴയ കഥകൾ പറഞ്ഞുതരാൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.180; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"काम्यकं प्राप्य कौन्तेया युधिष्ठिरपुरोगमाः ।\nकृतातिथ्या मुनिगणैर्निषेदुः सह कृष्णया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached Kamyaka, the sons of Kunti, led by Yudhishthira, were hosted by bands of sages and sat down together with Krishna."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततस्तान्परिविश्वस्तान्वसतः पाण्डुनन्दनान् ।\nब्राह्मणा बहवस्तत्र समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as the sons of Pandu settled in with confidence, many brahmins gathered around them on every side."}},{"n":3,"text":"अथाब्रवीद्द्विजः कश्चिदर्जुनस्य प्रियः सखा ।\nएष्यतीह महाबाहुर्वशी शौरिरुदारधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a brahmin who was a dear friend of Arjuna said, \"The mighty-armed, self-controlled and noble-minded Shauri will come here."}},{"n":4,"text":"विदिता हि हरेर्यूयमिहायाताः कुरूद्वहाः ।\nसदा हि दर्शनाकाङ्क्षी श्रेयोऽन्वेषी च वो हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hari knows that you, bearers of the Kuru line, have come here, for he always longs to see you and seeks your good."}},{"n":5,"text":"बहुवत्सरजीवी च मार्कण्डेयो महातपाः ।\nस्वाध्यायतपसा युक्तः क्षिप्रं युष्मान्समेष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Markandeya, of great austerity, who has lived many years and is devoted to study and penance, will quickly meet you.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"तथैव तस्य ब्रुवतः प्रत्यदृश्यत केशवः ।\nसैन्यसुग्रीवयुक्तेन रथेन रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even as he spoke, Keshava, best of charioteers, appeared in a chariot yoked with Saibya and Sugriva."}},{"n":7,"text":"मघवानिव पौलोम्या सहितः सत्यभामया ।\nउपायाद्देवकीपुत्रो दिदृक्षुः कुरुसत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like Indra with Paulomi, Devaki's son came with Satyabhama, wishing to see the best of the Kurus."}},{"n":8,"text":"अवतीर्य रथात्कृष्णो धर्मराजं यथाविधि ।\nववन्दे मुदितो धीमान्भीमं च बलिनां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Getting down from the chariot, Krishna, glad and wise, bowed to the king of dharma as is proper, and to Bhima, best of the strong."}},{"n":9,"text":"पूजयामास धौम्यं च यमाभ्यामभिवादितः ।\nपरिष्वज्य गुडाकेशं द्रौपदीं पर्यसान्त्वयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He honored Dhaumya and was greeted by the twins. He embraced Gudakesha and consoled Draupadi."}},{"n":10,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा फल्गुनं वीरं चिरस्य प्रियमागतम् ।\nपर्यष्वजत दाशार्हः पुनः पुनररिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the hero Phalguna after a long time, the dear one come back, the Dasharha embraced him again and again, tamer of foes."}},{"n":11,"text":"तथैव सत्यभामापि द्रौपदीं परिषस्वजे ।\nपाण्डवानां प्रियां भार्यां कृष्णस्य महिषी प्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Satyabhama embraced Draupadi, the Pandavas' beloved wife, she being Krishna's dear queen."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्ते पाण्डवाः सर्वे सभार्याः सपुरोहिताः ।\nआनर्चुः पुण्डरीकाक्षं परिवव्रुश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Pandavas with their wives and their priest honored the lotus-eyed one and gathered around him on every side."}},{"n":13,"text":"कृष्णस्तु पार्थेन समेत्य विद्वा-\nन्धनंजयेनासुरतर्जनेन ।\nबभौ यथा भूतपतिर्महात्मा\nसमेत्य साक्षाद्भगवान्गुहेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, the wise, meeting Partha Dhananjaya, who had cowed the asuras, shone like the great-souled lord of beings meeting the blessed Guha himself."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः समस्तानि किरीटमाली\nवनेषु वृत्तानि गदाग्रजाय ।\nउक्त्वा यथावत्पुनरन्वपृच्छ-\nत्कथं सुभद्रा च तथाभिमन्युः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wearer of the diadem told Krishna, the elder brother of Gada, all that had happened in the forests, and asked in turn about Subhadra and Abhimanyu."}},{"n":15,"text":"स पूजयित्वा मधुहा यथाव-\nत्पार्थांश्च कृष्णां च पुरोहितं च ।\nउवाच राजानमभिप्रशंस-\nन्युधिष्ठिरं तत्र सहोपविश्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"The slayer of Madhu duly honored the Parthas, Krishna the princess and the priest, and, sitting there, spoke in praise of King Yudhishthira."}},{"n":16,"text":"धर्मः परः पाण्डव राज्यलाभा-\nत्तस्यार्थमाहुस्तप एव राजन् ।\nसत्यार्जवाभ्यां चरता स्वधर्मं\nजितस्तवायं च परश्च लोकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dharma is higher than the winning of a kingdom, Pandava, and they say austerity is the means to it, O king. By living your own dharma with truth and honesty, you have conquered both this world and the next."}},{"n":17,"text":"अधीतमग्रे चरता व्रतानि\nसम्यग्धनुर्वेदमवाप्य कृत्स्नम् ।\nक्षात्रेण धर्मेण वसूनि लब्ध्वा\nसर्वे ह्यवाप्ताः क्रतवः पुराणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You studied first while keeping vows, rightly mastered the whole science of archery, won wealth by the warrior's dharma, and performed all the ancient sacrifices."}},{"n":18,"text":"न ग्राम्यधर्मेषु रतिस्तवास्ति\nकामान्न किंचित्कुरुषे नरेन्द्र ।\nन चार्थलोभात्प्रजहासि धर्मं\nतस्मात्स्वभावादसि धर्मराजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You take no delight in worldly pleasures and do nothing out of desire, lord of men, and you do not give up dharma from greed for wealth. So you are king of dharma by nature."}},{"n":19,"text":"दानं च सत्यं च तपश्च राज-\nञ्श्रद्धा च शान्तिश्च धृतिः क्षमा च ।\nअवाप्य राष्ट्राणि वसूनि भोगा-\nनेषा परा पार्थ सदा रतिस्ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charity, truth, austerity, faith, calm, steadiness and forbearance: even after gaining kingdoms, wealth and enjoyments, this is always your highest delight, Partha."}},{"n":20,"text":"यदा जनौघः कुरुजाङ्गलानां\nकृष्णां सभायामवशामपश्यत् ।\nअपेतधर्मव्यवहारवृत्तं\nसहेत तत्पाण्डव कस्त्वदन्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the crowd of the people of Kurujangala saw Draupadi helpless in the assembly, the abandonment of all conduct by dharma, who other than you, Pandava, could have borne it?"}},{"n":21,"text":"असंशयं सर्वसमृद्धकामः\nक्षिप्रं प्रजाः पालयितासि सम्यक् ।\nइमे वयं निग्रहणे कुरूणां\nयदि प्रतिज्ञा भवतः समाप्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without doubt, with all your wishes fulfilled, you will soon protect your subjects well. We are here to punish the Kurus, if your vow is complete.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"धौम्यं च कृष्णां च युधिष्ठिरं च\nयमौ च भीमं च दशार्हसिंहः ।\nउवाच दिष्ट्या भवतां शिवेन\nप्राप्तः किरीटी मुदितः कृतास्त्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lion of the Dasharhas said to Dhaumya, Draupadi, Yudhishthira, the twins and Bhima, \"By good fortune the wearer of the diadem has come back safe, glad, and a master of weapons.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रोवाच कृष्णामपि याज्ञसेनीं\nदशार्हभर्ता सहितः सुहृद्भिः ।\nकृष्णे धनुर्वेदरतिप्रधानाः\nसत्यव्रतास्ते शिशवः सुशीलाः ।\nसद्भिः सदैवाचरितं समाधिं\nचरन्ति पुत्रास्तव याज्ञसेनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of the Dasharhas, with his friends, also spoke to Draupadi, the Yajnasena's daughter: \"Krishna, your sons are eager for archery, true to their vows, young and well behaved."}},{"n":24,"text":"राज्येन राष्ट्रैश्च निमन्त्र्यमाणाः\nपित्रा च कृष्णे तव सोदरैश्च ।\nन यज्ञसेनस्य न मातुलानां\nगृहेषु बाला रतिमाप्नुवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They follow the discipline always practiced by the good, Draupadi. Though invited by their father and by your brothers with kingdom and territory, the boys find no delight in Yajnasena's house nor in their uncles'."}},{"n":25,"text":"आनर्तमेवाभिमुखाः शिवेन\nगत्वा धनुर्वेदरतिप्रधानाः ।\nतवात्मजा वृष्णिपुरं प्रविश्य\nन दैवतेभ्यः स्पृहयन्ति कृष्णे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going happily toward Anarta, entering Vrishni's city, those sons of yours, devoted above all to archery, have no longing for anything else, Krishna."}},{"n":26,"text":"यथा त्वमेवार्हसि तेषु वृत्तिं\nप्रयोक्तुमार्या च यथैव कुन्ती ।\nतेष्वप्रमादेन सदा करोति\nतथा च भूयश्च तथा सुभद्रा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you yourself would deserve in dealing with them, and as the noble Kunti would, so Subhadra always takes care of them, without negligence, and even more so."}},{"n":27,"text":"यथानिरुद्धस्य यथाभिमन्यो-\nर्यथा सुनीथस्य यथैव भानोः ।\nतथा विनेता च गतिश्च कृष्णे\nतवात्मजानामपि रौक्मिणेयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As for Aniruddha, Abhimanyu, Sunitha and Bhanu, so for your sons, Krishna, Rukmini's son Pradyumna is their guide and refuge."}},{"n":28,"text":"गदासिचर्मग्रहणेषु शूरा-\nनस्त्रेषु शिक्षासु रथाश्वयाने ।\nसम्यग्विनेता विनयत्यतन्द्री-\nस्तांश्चाभिमन्युः सततं कुमारः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In handling mace, sword and shield, in weapons and training, in chariot and horse driving, young Abhimanyu always trains them well, keeping them from idleness."}},{"n":29,"text":"स चापि सम्यक्प्रणिधाय शिक्षा-\nमस्त्राणि चैषां गुरुवत्प्रदाय ।\nतवात्मजानां च तथाभिमन्योः\nपराक्रमैस्तुष्यति रौक्मिणेयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Pradyumna, having arranged their training properly and given them weapons like a teacher, is pleased by the valor of your sons and of Abhimanyu."}},{"n":30,"text":"यदा विहारं प्रसमीक्षमाणाः\nप्रयान्ति पुत्रास्तव याज्ञसेनि ।\nएकैकमेषामनुयान्ति तत्र\nरथाश्च यानानि च दन्तिनश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"When your sons go out, Draupadi, to see the sport, chariots, vehicles and elephants follow each one of them."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथाब्रवीद्धर्मराजं तु कृष्णो\nदशार्हयोधाः कुकुरान्धकाश्च ।\nएते निदेशं तव पालयन्ति\nतिष्ठन्ति यत्रेच्छसि तत्र राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna said to the king of dharma, \"The Dasharha warriors, the Kukuras and the Andhakas obey your command. They stay wherever you wish, O king."}},{"n":32,"text":"आवर्ततां कार्मुकवेगवाता\nहलायुधप्रग्रहणा मधूनाम् ।\nसेना तवार्थेषु नरेन्द्र यत्ता\nससादिपत्त्यश्वरथा सनागा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the army of the Madhus turn out, with the force of bows like a gale and ploughs in their hands, striving for your cause, lord of men, with horsemen, foot soldiers, horses, chariots and elephants."}},{"n":33,"text":"प्रस्थाप्यतां पाण्डव धार्तराष्ट्रः\nसुयोधनः पापकृतां वरिष्ठः ।\nस सानुबन्धः ससुहृद्गणश्च\nसौभस्य सौभाधिपतेश्च मार्गम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Send out Duryodhana, Dhritarashtra's son, best of wrongdoers, with his followers and his friends, along the path of Saubha and the lord of Saubha."}},{"n":34,"text":"कामं तथा तिष्ठ नरेन्द्र तस्मि-\nन्यथा कृतस्ते समयः सभायाम् ।\nदाशार्हयोधैस्तु ससादियोधं\nप्रतीक्षतां नागपुरं भवन्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stay here, lord of men, as you wish, according to the pact you made in the assembly; let Nagapura await you, with its cavalry, by the Dasharha warriors."}},{"n":35,"text":"व्यपेतमन्युर्व्यपनीतपाप्मा\nविहृत्य यत्रेच्छसि तत्र कामम् ।\nततः समृद्धं प्रथमं विशोकः\nप्रपत्स्यसे नागपुरं सराष्ट्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Free of anger, with your sins washed away, stay as you wish and enjoy yourself; and then, free of sorrow, you will first reach prosperous Nagapura with its realm.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"ततस्तदाज्ञाय मतं महात्मा\nयथावदुक्तं पुरुषोत्तमेन ।\nप्रशस्य विप्रेक्ष्य च धर्मराजः\nकृताञ्जलिः केशवमित्युवाच ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled king of dharma, understanding Krishna's view as it was properly stated by the best of men, praised it and looked at him, and with joined palms said this to Keshava."}},{"n":37,"text":"असंशयं केशव पाण्डवानां\nभवान्गतिस्त्वच्छरणा हि पार्थाः ।\nकालोदये तच्च ततश्च भूयः\nकर्ता भवान्कर्म न संशयोऽस्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Without doubt, Keshava, you are the refuge of the Pandavas, for the Parthas have you as shelter. When the time comes, you will do what is to be done, no doubt."}},{"n":38,"text":"यथाप्रतिज्ञं विहृतश्च कालः\nसर्वाः समा द्वादश निर्जनेषु ।\nअज्ञातचर्यां विधिवत्समाप्य\nभवद्गताः केशव पाण्डवेयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As promised, the time has been spent, all twelve years in lonely places. Having duly finished the year of living unknown, the Pandavas will come to you, Keshava.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"तथा वदति वार्ष्णेये धर्मराजे च भारत ।\nअथ पश्चात्तपोवृद्धो बहुवर्षसहस्रधृक् ।\nप्रत्यदृश्यत धर्मात्मा मार्कण्डेयो महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Vrishni's descendant and the king of dharma were speaking so, O Bharata, afterward the righteous, great ascetic Markandeya, ripe in austerity and bearing many thousands of years, appeared."}},{"n":40,"text":"तमागतमृषिं वृद्धं बहुवर्षसहस्रिणम् ।\nआनर्चुर्ब्राह्मणाः सर्वे कृष्णश्च सह पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the brahmins and Krishna, with the Pandavas, honored the aged sage, who had lived many thousands of years, when he came."}},{"n":41,"text":"तमर्चितं सुविश्वस्तमासीनमृषिसत्तमम् ।\nब्राह्मणानां मतेनाह पाण्डवानां च केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the best of sages was honored and was seated at ease, Keshava said to him, with the approval of the brahmins and the Pandavas,"}},{"n":42,"text":"शुश्रूषवः पाण्डवास्ते ब्राह्मणाश्च समागताः ।\nद्रौपदी सत्यभामा च तथाहं परमं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Pandavas are eager to listen, and the brahmins are assembled, and Draupadi and Satyabhama and I too, for the highest words."}},{"n":43,"text":"पुरावृत्ताः कथाः पुण्याः सदाचाराः सनातनाः ।\nराज्ञां स्त्रीणामृषीणां च मार्कण्डेय विचक्ष्व नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya, tell us ancient, holy stories of conduct that is always good and eternal, about kings, women and sages.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"तेषु तत्रोपविष्टेषु देवर्षिरपि नारदः ।\nआजगाम विशुद्धात्मा पाण्डवानवलोककः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they sat there, the divine sage Narada too, pure in soul, came, wishing to see the Pandavas."}},{"n":45,"text":"तमप्यथ महात्मानं सर्वे तु पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nपाद्यार्घ्याभ्यां यथान्यायमुपतस्थुर्मनीषिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the foremost men, in due form, attended that great-souled wise one with water for the feet and the offering."}},{"n":46,"text":"नारदस्त्वथ देवर्षिर्ज्ञात्वा तांस्तु कृतक्षणान् ।\nमार्कण्डेयस्य वदतस्तां कथामन्वमोदत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the divine sage Narada, seeing that they were at leisure, approved the story Markandeya was telling."}},{"n":47,"text":"उवाच चैनं कालज्ञः स्मयन्निव स नारदः ।\nब्रह्मर्षे कथ्यतां यत्ते पाण्डवेषु विवक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the time, Narada, smiling a little, said to him, \"Brahmin sage, say what you intended to say to the Pandavas.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच मार्कण्डेयो महातपाः ।\nक्षणं कुरुध्वं विपुलमाख्यातव्यं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the great ascetic Markandeya answered, \"Wait a moment; there is a great deal to tell.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"एवमुक्ताः क्षणं चक्रुः पाण्डवाः सह तैर्द्विजैः ।\nमध्यंदिने यथादित्यं प्रेक्षन्तस्तं महामुनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So told, the Pandavas and those brahmins waited a moment, looking at the great sage as at the sun at midday."}}]}]}